Dear Sir or Madam,

Further to Andrea Keller's first notice of Friday 28 August (your claim no. P=
IQ-S-2026-082814, policy PIQ-CH-KMU-2026-048213), please find attached our si=
gned claim form (Schadenmeldung) and six photos.

Demo map anchor: Steinberggasse 23, 8400 Winterthur. The address is real; the=
 business, premises and loss are fictional. AI images do not depict the actua=
l building or its occupants. Street View shows the real location, not these d=
amage scenes.

Our provisional consolidated loss estimate amounts to CHF 1,697,400.00:
- Building items: shop window glazing, workshop skylight, awning and facade p=
anels: CHF 184,000.00
- Stock in the shop and storeroom (pralines, bars, autumn and Christmas stock=
, packaging): CHF 312,500.00
- Refrigerated goods in the cold room: CHF 96,400.00
- Production equipment (two tempering machines, enrobing machine, cooling tun=
nel, moulding line): CHF 486,000.00
- Shop fittings (counter, display cases, chilled display, lighting, till syst=
em): CHF 168,000.00
- Business interruption, September to December 2026 (Christmas season): CHF 3=
98,000.00
- Clean-up, disposal, emergency glazing and drying: CHF 52,500.00

A few points for your assessment:

1. The main fuse tripped during the storm; the emergency electrician addition=
ally isolated the supply on 28 August at 11:30. Power was restored on 29 Augu=
st at 15:00. The photo at 15:04 shows a 23.8 =C2=B0C readout shortly after re=
storation. We report the refrigerated contents as lost because of the interru=
pted cold chain, subject to temperature-record and food-safety review. We und=
erstand that our policy may not include the refrigerated goods extension; as =
the power cut was a direct consequence of the hailstorm, we ask you to consid=
er this loss as part of the storm damage.

2. The property management has also reported the building damage to the GVZ (=
GVZ claim no. 2026-08-4471). We renewed the shop window and the skylight ours=
elves in 2019 as tenant improvements, which is why we include them here.

3. The photo dated Wednesday 26 August (18:34) shows selected shop-window sto=
ck two days before the storm. It is not damage evidence or proof of the compl=
ete inventory.

Photographic evidence and limits:
The photos show selected stock and damage, not the full inventory or its valu=
e. In the scenario the awning was retracted before the storm. Wind-driven hai=
l struck the exposed facade obliquely from above. The laminated glazing in th=
e shop window and rooflight is cracked but retained on its interlayer: no pun=
ched-out holes or open glass breaches.
Reported water ingress is through storm-loosened frame joints, not solid glaz=
ing. Wet tracks are local to the shop-window corner and one rooflight-frame j=
oint in the single-storey rear annex; the cause and extent of leaks require t=
echnical assessment. No external emergency cover is present at 11:26. The tem=
pering bowl has its normal closed food-protection lid; stock, pralines and in=
gredients are in closed packaging, showcases or covered containers. Cracked g=
lass alone does not establish contamination of all stock.
One tempering machine is externally wet; the reported short circuit and repai=
r scope of all equipment require technical assessment. The hail ruler is an i=
llustrative size reference, not a calibrated measurement.
The cold-room photo shows selected stock and a 23.8 =C2=B0C readout shortly a=
fter power restoration, not the temperature history or microbiological proof =
of spoilage. Cartons in the intact cold room are dry. The insured reports ref=
rigerated-stock loss because of the interrupted cold chain; temperature recor=
ds and food-safety assessment remain necessary.
All amounts are provisional demands. Inventory lists, technical reports, temp=
erature records, quotes and business records are not attached.

Inventory lists as at 31 July 2026, our September to December sales figures f=
or 2024 and 2025 and the contractors' quotes will follow by 11 September.

Thank you for scheduling the loss adjuster's visit on Friday 4 September 2026=
 at 09:00; we will be on site.

Kind regards,

